# Phase 3.5 CLI acceptance — counting surface completion (W4, D-3.5-06).
#
# Segment 4 of 4 (host-backed, D-13): the segment-3 database has an active
# edition with derived forms and no morphology dataset. This segment proves
# the remaining counting verbs are reachable from the CLI with their rules
# blocks, and that the zero-proof verb carries its disclaimer.
#
# Fixture-scale evidence only; the full-corpus run stays OD-11-gated
# (see docs/05-followups/phase-3.5-deferrals.md).

```console
$ qai quran count distribution ويت --profile L3.diacritics
ويت: 3 occurrence(s) across 3 surah(s); partitions keyed by surah number (canonical structure)

```

```console
$ qai quran count occurrences ويت --profile L3.diacritics
first Some((1, 3)), last Some((5, 3)), span Some(12)
Intervals describe ayah positions only; no chronological or interpretive claim is made.

```

```console
$ qai quran count cooccurrence ويت --profile L3.diacritics
co-occurrence within token:3 — 10 candidate(s)

```

```console
$ qai quran count collocation ويت --profile L3.diacritics
collocations (LLR-ranked) — 2 candidate(s)

```

```console
$ qai quran count numeric-report ويت --profile L3.diacritics
ويت: 3
Numeric output only; no interpretive commentary is provided.

```

```console
$ qai quran count missing-form zzqqxxnotaword --profile L3.diacritics
zzqqxxnotaword: 0 occurrence(s) under L3.diacritics
Absence under these counting rules is not evidence of absence under other rules; see the CountingRules block.

```

```console
$ qai quran count near-duplicates
near-duplicates (>= 0.8) — 3 pair(s)

```

